// audit-ci configuration for TaskBuddy CI (task A6).
//
// Runs `npm audit` and FAILS the build on any advisory at moderate severity or
// above that is NOT in the allowlist below. This turns `npm audit` into a
// meaningful gate (it catches NEW vulnerabilities) instead of permanent red
// noise from known dev/build-only advisories.
//
// Usage in CI (add to .github/workflows/ci.yml after the build step):
//   - name: Security audit (allowlisted)
//     run: npx --yes audit-ci@^7 --config ./audit-ci.jsonc
//
// The allowlist mirrors the "Accepted" dependency findings (DEP-02..DEP-06) in
// .do_not_upload/security_assessment.md. DEP-02..DEP-05 are dev/build/test only
// and not reachable in the running service. DEP-01 (nodemailer runtime advisory,
// GHSA-p6gq-j5cr-w38f) was FIXED (nodemailer@^9), NOT allowlisted — if it ever
// regresses, CI must fail. DEP-06 (GHSA-8988, otel baggage) is a RUNTIME advisory
// that IS allowlisted as a time-boxed, owner-approved risk acceptance because no
// compatible fix exists yet (details by its allowlist entry below).
//
// RE-TRIAGE: remove an entry here when a non-downgrade patch lands upstream, or
// when an advisory escalates to critical / moves into the runtime path. Keep
// this file and security_assessment.md (§ Dependency Audit) in sync.
{
  // Fail on moderate, high, and critical advisories (anything not allowlisted).
  "moderate": true,

  "allowlist": [
    // DEP-02 — serialize-javascript RCE, via workbox-build -> next-pwa@5 (PWA BUILD only).
    "GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq",

    // DEP-03 — postcss XSS, vendored inside next (CSS BUILD only).
    "GHSA-qx2v-qp2m-jg93",

    // DEP-04 — minimatch ReDoS x3, via @typescript-eslint -> eslint-config-next@14 (LINT only).
    "GHSA-3ppc-4f35-3m26",
    "GHSA-7r86-cg39-jmmj",
    "GHSA-23c5-xmqv-rm74",

    // DEP-05 (js-yaml DoS, GHSA-h67p-54hq-rp68) REMOVED 2026-07-21 — the advisory no longer
    // appears in `npm audit`, so the entry was dead. A dead entry is not harmless: it would
    // silently suppress the same advisory if a future dependency reintroduced it.

    // DEP-06 — @opentelemetry/core: unbounded memory allocation in W3C Baggage propagation
    // (moderate, CVSS 5.3, CWE-770). RUNTIME advisory, transitive via
    // @sentry/node@9.47.1 -> bundled @opentelemetry/* -> @opentelemetry/core@1.30.1 (A4).
    // NO COMPATIBLE FIX: the patch is only in @opentelemetry/core >= 2.8.0 (a major bump);
    // Sentry 9.47.1 pins otel core ^1.30.1 across its 1.x SDK packages, and there is no 1.x
    // backport, so forcing 2.8.0 would break Sentry's runtime.
    // ACCEPTED RISK (owner-approved 2026-07-01), mitigated by: Node's default 16KB
    // max-http-header-size bounding the `baggage` header, Cloudflare in front, global rate
    // limiting, and tracesSampleRate=0. RE-TRIAGE: remove when @sentry/node depends on
    // @opentelemetry/core >= 2.8.0. See security_assessment.md § Dependency Audit.
    "GHSA-8988-4f7v-96qf"
  ]
}
